    "body": "Finding (SKULL worker, held; no PR opened yet): the fix works on its own streams, but it moves a golden. The six-post fix is on `mkinney:issue/1028-cycle-seat-latent` (c5e931c6, stacked on #1019). It adds the hop seat with a named refusal when no `RetractPlane` is stated, plus `probeSeat()` on the probe hooks. It is pinned by 4 new `cycle_hop` tests, and each fails with #1019's posts.\n\nThe full quick gate (`--base upstream/main`) is 2218 passed, 1 failed: `conformance::the_synthesized_stream_locks_the_tool_and_spindle_words`.\n- Its test-built `synth_stream_with` stream is exactly the case this issue names: back-to-back cycle records, no leaving rapids, and no `RetractPlane` PARAM.\n- So all six cycle posts now refuse it by name. Before this change, `synth_fanuc.nc` lines 13-30 traversed between holes at R (`G00 Z-3`, then `G00 X50 Y30` ...).\n\nMaking it pass means moving the `synth_*` goldens. Either add `RetractPlane` to the synth stream (the goldens gain hop climbs), or give the synth stream leaving rapids. The worker's brief said to stop when a golden moves, so this waits for the manager's call. The claim stays with SKULL.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
